      "placeholders": {
        "MATH_0001": "$\\NL_{X/B}$",
        "MATH_0002": "$D_\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X)$",
        "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{F}) \\longrightarrow\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{G})\n$$",
        "MATH_0004": "$i$",
        "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{F}$",
        "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{G}$",
        "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-netherlander-quasi-coherent}",
        "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-huge-diagram-ringed-topoi}",
        "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-choices-ringed-topoi}"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{proof}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:4ee1cdf5311eff108e2e1b009e81c9f982f40ab5aedd9834828a244ca217698b",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a5d272bf80d62bd07c44378a956829f07d714e68584cbce7386cd5d7d80051e",
      "source_text": "Recall that <MATH_0001> is an object of <MATH_0002>, see\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nHence our assumption implies the maps\n<MATH_0003>\nare isomorphisms for all <MATH_0004>. This implies our functor is fully\nfaithful by Lemma <REF_0002>.\nOn the other hand, the functor is essentially surjective by\nLemma <REF_0003> because\nwe have the solutions <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> in both categories.\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:4bba49b5b4c2bbe1360c8c0190c7113be8ff588f48f9570c9aab4cf6c6f21fde",
